From 369010dd567283d6490a3fe6fd13fea0388d6be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:07:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] ##arch: Emulate the USSE forms of the third probe round

A third round of client fills on an SGX545 pinned the colour, integer
dot product and expanded float groups, and the ESIL follows the answers.
Colour channels are bytes, byte 3 the alpha, x standing for x / 255:

- sop2, sop3, lrp1, lrp2, sop2wm on 8-bit operands: add/sub sum the
  exact products, divide by 255 once, round and saturate; min/max compare
  the sources; asat, s2scale, zeros, comp and neg as measured; lerps by
  s0/s0a; sop2wm's byte mask
- u8dot3/4, u16dot3/4 and the off forms: the byte products summed, scaled
  by Cx/Ax, rounded and saturated, u16 as a 15-bit fraction in both
  halves; u8dot3's aadd/asub/aintrp1/aintrp2 alpha
- fpma = c0 + c1 c2 on 8-bit channels
- efo: the printed dataflow, products and sums rounded to binary32, the
  destination's i0/i1 read before the writes (not .gpiext, which reaches
  other instances' internal registers for one pixel in four)
- fadm = a.c + b.c, fmsa = a.a + b.c, fsubflr = a - floor(b)
- statomic and movmsk .smsk

The helpers evaluate each operand once with DUP/SWAP: ESIL keeps stacked
strings in a ring, and a value left on the stack while hundreds of others
are pushed is overwritten. c10 and half-float operands, repeats, fmad16
and the transcendental functions stay unmodelled.

8 new and 1 changed test/db/esil/usse tests. The microkernel uses none of
these forms: 84.2% of its words still have ESIL; 527 of 153466 decodable
random words do (was 425).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
